    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/4/4/44975.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 9,
    "turn_text": "Well, it was pretty simple. I saw the direction that things were headed in Washington, D.C. The writing was on the wall. And I think we're actually seeing a lot of that play out now with the policies that the Democrats are pushing forward in Washington, D.C. But I said, hey, this is a really important time to stand up for the future of our country. I'm 38 years old. I'll be 39 this summer. But I think about truly that next generation and making sure that They can be successful and having good people there to be your advocate is crucial. And so when my husband and I had that conversation about, hey, I really think I should step up and add my mom with the minivan and a mortgage voice to the conversation. We just need some common sense people in Washington. And so that's why I said, hey, I will, I think it's my time to step up and do this. And I'm very excited that we crossed the finish line first. It was a hard fought battle and but we were able to be successful and came very close to taking back the house and I think that's our main goal this year in November. Oh",
