  {
    "episode_id": 44975,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/4/4/44975.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 11,
    "turn_text": "Oh, well, I think just the sheer volume of policy that moves in Washington DC. I mean, the number of bills that are introduced, it is thousands upon thousands. So, you know, when I found out, obviously you have, you know, more than a dozen staff who are working for you to help you sort through all that it's. It's mountains and mountains of policy. So that I think was one of the things that I found most, I would say surprising about going to Washington DC. But what I think is important is surrounding yourself with the right people to vet that policy for you and making sure that Iowans have a chance to have all that policy vetted. So that's in my mind kind of one of the things that I was surprised by, but now I've figured out a good system to work through as well.",
    "speaker_id": "SPEAKER_01",
