    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/4/4/44975.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 13,
    "turn_text": "nothing quite prepares you for for serving in Congress, certainly in Washington, BC. It's already a completely chaotic place. But I think, you know, the dysfunction is undersold. You know, you hear about things on the five o'clock news and then you get to see them play out in real time on the dysfunction on the floor. over the last year, obviously a lot of the COVID restrictions have still been in place. So we've really gotten a chance to see that that chaos play out, but you can't undersell that. It's a real lesson in patients in terms of going there and working through the process. But I think that chaos, I knew it was going to be bad, but it's really bad in Washington.",
