    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/4/4/44975.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 20,
    "turn_text": "Well, like I said, it's really important that we have strong common sense conservatives willing to stand up for the shared values that we all have. I firmly believe, you know, Iowa values are heartland values and heartland values are American values and that's why we need more conservative women to step up and run. And I was part of a record breaking freshman class of GOP women and And you look at the success that we've had in just the first little over a year that we've been in office. It does show that having a variety of perspectives in Congress really is important a variety of backgrounds and I think women have a lot to add to that conversation. in several cases to have conversations with some of my colleagues and actually change their minds and say, hey, here's my perspective on this as a woman in the workplace, as a mom. And I think adding that extra context is what our founding fathers really would have wanted to see, right? And so I think that's why we need more conservative women to step up and run.",
