    "turn_text": "step up and run. First of all, I think everybody always wants to come up with an excuse, right? Oh, well, now is not a good time because, well, I'd say either one, let's eliminate the because and let's try and get it to a place where you can step up and run. Or in my case, my husband and I talked and there's never really a good time to do anything in life, right? You just have to take those risks and be willing to jump for what you think is important. And that's exactly what I've chosen to do. I also I'm a very faithful person and I believe God gives you what you can handle. And sometimes what you can handle is challenging, but I believe that that's all by design. So I would encourage everyone to step up and add their ways to the conversation, how they think they can. and challenge yourself to get a little out of your comfort zone. You know, it's just really important and risk is rewarded, but the answer is always no if you don't ask and that's what I think is really important. So my favorite piece of scripture is actually in the book of Matthew where it's the ask, seek, knock. You know, if you ask, you'll get an answer. If you seek, you'll find and if you knock the door will open and",
