    "turn_idx": 31,
    "turn_text": "you know, I obviously highlighted some of the backgrounds and why that matters, you know, I like to call it context perspective and relevance, having all of the CPR, so to speak, makes a really, really good candidate, but it really comes down to helping to build our bench. We need people with experience with a variety of these backgrounds. to be in the pipeline to step up and run for opportunities as they present themselves. So every level of recruitment, whether it's the school wards, we've seen a lot of success, obviously, in making sure parents voices are now reflected on school wards, state legislatures and state Senate's state houses, then moving to Congress, right, to build up our party and continue to make sure we are securing the future of this common conservative vision. That's why having such a solid bench and good solid candidates recruited is absolutely critical and I have conversations with a lot of conservative women friends of mine and I'm saying, hey, you should step up and add your voice because They're concerned about the future of our country and we're having those conversations. So I'm trying to do my part to make sure they feel like they could do it and they could step up to run. And again, let's eliminate that. Well, I can't because let's do it. I have to because it's important.",
