    "turn_idx": 36,
    "turn_text": "Yeah. Well, I think being authentic is absolutely critical to being a good public leader. And people want to know that the person representing them isn't, you know, sitting in a back room, ignoring their conversations. And I think that if you can add that level of authenticity, it adds credibility to the fact that you're serving in Washington or wherever you're serving in the state house. or your city council that, hey, I know what everybody's experiencing. I'm pulling in that context. I'm not afraid to listen. I think that's where all that authenticity can really make a difference in making sure you have the right candidate and making sure as a candidate you are also connecting with voters in a very meaningful way.",
