    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/4/4/44975.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 41,
    "turn_text": "Well, I think It's interesting because we've kind of undergone just a massive expansion of our party in terms of who we are reaching out to. And I think that's because the Democrat Party has turned its backs on people. So Republicans, we're welcoming people to our big tent party. Just recently, the head of the Democrat Party said that Republicans are frauds and fascists and I mean you talk about divisive rhetoric, I mean that is truly divisive and I think people are realizing that the Democrat party has left them behind the Democrat party is the party of big government and is taking our country towards socialism so I think that when we talk about moving forward as a party, people are tired of identity politics. Oh, because I'm a woman, I should be a liberal. Well, no, I'm especially a woman, former member of the media, right? No, I'm a conservative mom, like, and there's nothing wrong with that. And I have been a conservative my entire life. And I think that what we're going to start seeing is that, hey, just because you look a certain way or have a certain background that doesn't tie you to a political ideology, And so I think it's a great opportunity for us as a party to reach out to people who, hey, we are fighting for you on this issue. We're fighting for you on this issue and we're fighting for you on this issue. And we don't have to agree on everything, but let us tell you why we believe our solutions are the best option. And I think that that's why we're moving forward and we have a lot of great opportunity as a party going forward.",
